Sometimes it is not enough to only filter exceptions by exception class. 

This adds `dontReportUsing` to the Exceptions class to allow you to register a callback that can inspect exceptions to determine if you want them to be reported. 

**Example usage:**
```php
// In bootstrap/app.php

$app = Application::configure(basePath: dirname(__DIR__))
    ->withExceptions(function (Exceptions $exceptions) {
        $exceptions->dontReportUsing(function (Throwable $e) {
            if ($e instanceof PaymentErrorApiException && in_array($e->getErrorCode(), [
                'incorrect_card_number',
                'incorrect_cvc',
                'insufficient_funds',
                'transaction_not_allowed',
                'card_expired',
                'card_not_supported',
            ], true)) {
                return true;
            }
        });
    })->create();
```

I'll also add documentation for this if accepted.

These are the changes I made to the frontend for the purposes of Charon over the last few weeks. In rough order, the changes looks like:
- Add an explicit `Self: Trait` clause to trait methods and consts (replaces https://github.com/cryspen/hax/pull/1541);
- Fix `ImplExpr::Builtin` that had some type errors (replaces https://github.com/cryspen/hax/pull/1543);
- Improve the translation of `Drop` information;
- Add variance information to type parameters (replaces https://github.com/cryspen/hax/pull/1547);
- Cleanup the `State` infrastructure a little bit (this is opinionated, you might disagree);
- Add information about the metadata to use in unsize coercions;
- Resolve `dyn Trait` predicates;
- Many improvements to `FullDef`;
- Add infrastructure to get a monomorphized `FullDef`; this is used in charon to monomorphize a crate graph.

I fixed `import_thir.ml` but not all the engine tests pass. I'll leave that to you.

The branch consists of a merge of about 10 branches that each could have been a PR; you can review merge-commit-by-merge-commit if you want, the bullet points above would be roughly the PR titles.

Added a shorter Menu to reduce print menu spam.
Added some comments for more readability.
Added the 5 functions asked to create, read, update and delete from table
> createCategory() : adds a category asking the user for input;
> listCategories() : lists all categories;
> createCategoryRecipes(): associates a category and a recipe;
> deleteCategoryRecipes() : removes the association between category and a recipe;
> listRecipesInCategory() : lists all recipes associated with a given category;

